{"id":101,"explanation":"Do not cache get_user results for the life of a process. After a role is revoked, a cached user could still have the old roles; fetching from the database avoids that stale result. #640 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":102,"explanation":"Check db.Query's error before calling defer rows.Close(). If the query fails, rows is nil, so trying to close it would be unsafe. The comment applies to the order of the three statements shown.","unsure":""}
{"id":103,"explanation":"Use setTimeout with a zero delay for this call to measure(el), rather than queueMicrotask. The stated reason is that layout must settle before the measurement runs.","unsure":""}
{"id":104,"explanation":"Do not log the contents of the Secret<String> token loaded here. Its Debug representation must reveal only a redacted value.","unsure":""}
{"id":105,"explanation":"Keep the RetryCount constant in sync with the Http.Retry setting in appsettings.json. Change both when changing the retry count. appsettings.json:Http.Retry names that file and setting.","unsure":""}
{"id":106,"explanation":"The offset passed to ch.map must be divisible by pageSize, with no remainder. Memory mapping rejects an offset that is not page aligned.","unsure":""}
{"id":107,"explanation":"The trailing slash in build/ makes rsync copy the contents of the build directory to $DEST, rather than copying the build directory itself. Preserve the slash if that is the intended result.","unsure":""}
{"id":108,"explanation":"The comment explains the BRIN index choice for events.created_at: it says the index is about 1% the size of a btree index, and the table receives rows in time order, which suits BRIN.","unsure":""}
{"id":109,"explanation":"Replace the shown spin loop, which repeatedly checks flag, with a futex based wait. The completion condition points to lock_acquire in src/sync/lock.c: it should sleep while waiting. That path and symbol identify where to check the change.","unsure":""}
{"id":110,"explanation":"The comment points to the failover section of the runbook for the reason dbo.RebuildStats runs on the secondary. doc:runbook#failover is a document anchor; the reason itself is not given in this snippet.","unsure":""}
{"id":111,"explanation":"Set this timeout below 60 seconds because an upstream proxy terminates idle requests after 60 seconds. The shown value, 30 seconds, satisfies that constraint.","unsure":""}
{"id":112,"explanation":"Keep Widget's destructor virtual. If it becomes non-virtual, deleting a derived object through a Widget pointer could skip the derived destructor. #915 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":113,"explanation":"Run PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON on each database connection before that connection performs any writes. The setting applies per connection, so enabling it elsewhere does not cover this one.","unsure":""}
{"id":114,"explanation":"Keep this field as the fixed-size Pascal ShortString form, string[40], rather than changing it to string. The containing record is written to disk byte for byte, so a different string representation would change the stored bytes.","unsure":""}
{"id":115,"explanation":"Treat p_id as caller supplied input and pass it through a bind variable, as USING p_id does for :1. Concatenating that input into the EXECUTE IMMEDIATE SQL text would permit SQL injection.","unsure":""}
